{"meta":{"ticker":"VCR","as_of_date":"2026-09-02","performance_as_of":"2026-08-31","generated_at":"2026-09-03 10:01:08"},"benchmark":{"ticker":"SPY","fund_name":"State Street SPDR S&P 500 ETF"},"overview":{"ticker":"VCR","fund_name":"Vanguard Consumer Discretionary ETF","category":"US Consumer Discretionary","issuer":"Vanguard","index_name":"MSCI US IMI 25/50 Consumer Discretionary","region":"North America","exchange":"NYSEARCA","expense_ratio":0.0009,"aum":5926207135,"holdings_count":287,"inception_date":"2004-01-26","overall_score":1.53710522123894,"overall_rank":1074,"sector_diversification_score":1.2713197487914},"description":{"tsi_description":"VCR is a consumer discretionary sector ETF that tracks the MSCI US Investable Market Consumer Discretionary 25/50 Index and provides exposure to U.S. companies across the large-, mid-, and small-cap spectrum. The fund uses a float-adjusted market-cap-weighting methodology with diversification constraints designed to limit excessive concentration among its largest holdings. Despite these constraints, VCR maintains substantial exposure to a small number of dominant consumer discretionary companies, resulting in a relatively concentrated portfolio profile. Compared to large-cap consumer discretionary ETFs, VCR offers broader exposure across sub-industries and market-cap segments through its all-cap construction approach. Overall, VCR offers diversified access to the U.S. consumer discretionary sector through a low-cost indexing framework.","strategy_steps":["Tracks the MSCI US Investable Market Consumer Discretionary 25/50 Index.","Invests in large-, mid-, and small-cap U.S. consumer discretionary companies classified under the GICS framework.","Uses a float-adjusted market-capitalization weighting methodology.","Applies a 25/50 diversification rule limiting individual security weights to 25% and aggregate weights above 5% to 50% of the portfolio.","Rebalances using tighter 22.5/45% thresholds to maintain compliance with d